# 7. DevOps Career Guidance

Key learning points from the session:

- Master Linux before learning advanced DevOps tools.
- Practice commands daily instead of only watching tutorials.
- Focus on interview preparation and practical troubleshooting.
- Learn to communicate and explain technical concepts clearly.
- Build projects and gain hands-on experience using AWS.

---

# Best Practices

- Practice Linux commands every day.
- Use AWS EC2 or a Virtual Machine for hands-on learning.
- Follow the Principle of Least Privilege when assigning permissions.
- Never use `chmod 777` in production unless absolutely necessary.
- Stop or terminate unused cloud resources to avoid unnecessary costs.

